  "title": "The locking rule and overlapping loops",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Proved by hand (with the advisor model): for harmonies stitched in one order, a closed chain of k knots locks its shared copies iff k is below the girth of the step relation (the hanging copy quantified away); the open chain is free at every length iff the relation has a step; figure eights are independent; through a shared knot a lock spreads but is never created. Exact: 495 of 495 and 495 of 495 cells; 75 of 75 figure eights and thetas; crossed pairs and circulants lock collectively; rings of overlapping knots lock by the arithmetic of their length. Referee pending.",
